Hi Andreas,

On 2019-04-08 12:50, Fuchs, Andreas wrote:
> I moved away from providing signed tar balls and only provide signed
> tags for release candidates for now.
> If you'd desire signed tar balls, please let me know and I'll start them =
again.

Does this apply only to release candidates, or to the final releases as
well?

- For the RCs, I don't mind at all.

- For the stable releases, it is somewhat convenient (but not critical)
to have (verifiable) distribution tarballs as this allows to skip
installing autoconf-archive and pandoc (since the files these generate
are already included in the tarball). This is especially nice in case of
pandoc with its many Haskell dependencies.

Kind regards,
Jonas


